Lev is a vampire of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] and a member of the [[Org/Althane/Oreskalka Cabal|Oreskalka Cabal]], whose seat is [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Umbervale Hold|Umbervale Hold]]. He trained at the hold and left it with his sire, on terms bad enough that the family could put a contract out on him. He would like to lead the cabal himself, and has been told that would take allies inside the family rather than strength.

He is a [[Org/Althane/Golden Sparrows|Golden Sparrow]] and has done the movement's killing. He murdered a writer in his own home for writing against the Sparrows, and he has killed a man in a train station with a single pencil. He is practiced at disguise and at playing a part, and keeps a folding cane among the odds and ends in his bag so he can pass as an old man.

Lev has bound himself to [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]]. He offered his life and his service as its sword in exchange for the destruction of [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the creature from below]], and Nox took the bargain. A strip of its black silk is fused to his arm, and when he bleeds out his blade now it comes black and wrapped in the same silk, trailing as he moves. While he keeps Nox's veil, he and those near him are hidden from scrying. The bond reaches deeper as time passes: a soul-scanner turned on him reads a quarter of his soul as the same black silk, and the rest of him is slowly taking on its bearing.

A blood relative of his in the cabal, [[People/Althane/Xanthin Oreskalka|Xanthin Oreskalka]], is dead, and Lev carries his still-beating heart. He says he killed him.

He travels with [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]], [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] and [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]] as [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]].
